# A rejected range-delete walk re-stamps under ANY open intent of the tree. The
# markers are range-scoped, so another intent's marker need not cover the leaves
# the walk's record reaches: a leaf that re-armed after the walk's own intent
# closed passes the record. Dropping L's marker from the guard stands for an open
# intent disjoint from L.
MODULE: ReadPositionHonestRestampUnderAnyIntent
TARGET: ReadPositionHonest
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a rejected walk re-stamps under any open intent, not only its own
PERTURBS: GRestamp
BOUNDS: WithTreeWalk = TRUE, WithBatch = FALSE, MaxWindows = 1

--- FIND
    /\ gst = "rejected"
    /\ hoOpen
    /\ ~closing
    /\ gst' = "repend"
--- REPLACE
    /\ gst = "rejected"
\* MUTATION: any open intent of the tree, not the walk's own.
    /\ ~closing
    /\ gst' = "repend"
--- END